I found another good way to solve it!

ui <- navbarPage(title = "test",id="appID",collapsible = TRUE,
                 tabPanel("Home"
                 ),
                 navbarMenu(title = "Production",
                            tabPanel("a",value = "production/a/"
                            ),
                            tabPanel("b",value="production/b/"
                            ),
                            tabPanel("c",value="production/c/"

server <- function(input, output){

  output$iframe<-renderUI({
    if(input$appID=="Home") tags$h1("Welcome to Home Page!")
    else
      tags$iframe(src = paste0("URURL",input$appID), seamless=TRUE,height="1000px", width="100%", scrolling="no")
  })

Here must be a tabpanel before navbarMenu, otherwise we will get weird bugs!

